data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1973,"item_id":"fc_01f024bb0dbc6f18016adb40514fe08191a976ff14d0dd05c6","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"6d2f5d8b91400bdc4399538836c54d930195c94289d939c88c3c3e29628f1b28\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual packet-only review; mathematical input boundary was packet.json and the declared Yui rules read for this task. No source proof, other inference body, or ambient premise was used. The first unsupported implication is in S001: from compactness of E to boundedness and then the assertion that cube coverings of a bounded Euclidean box imply dim_H(E)≤n. Compactness-implies-boundedness and the Hausdorff-dimension upper bound are not direct inputs or locally proved. Naming cube coverings does not establish the dimension theorem. This blocks the proof; later unsupported steps are diagnostic, not repairs. The packet's supplied packet_sha256 is reported as-is; carrier identity and canonical/transmitted-material binding are outside this mathematical review.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"H001 and H002 are listed direct inputs, and S001/S003 cite them. M001 and M002 are also listed direct inputs and are cited in S002 with explicit intended bindings. Presence of these inputs does not prove the unsupported S001 estimate.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\",\"/inference/argument/1/uses\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First failure: S001 asserts compact E is bounded and that cube coverings give D≤n without proving either the compactness/boundedness fact or the dimension estimate. It also asserts H^q(E)=0 from the definition and converts covers of E into product covers without establishing the needed Hausdorff-measure/dimension definitions and limiting argument. In S002 the key content-to-measure implications (H^s(E)=∞ implies scale contents tend to infinity; content comparison implies H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and the dimension lower bound) are asserted, not locally proved or supplied as inputs. S003 imports projection monotonicity of Hausdorff dimension and dim_H(I)=1 without proof or input. These are substantial theorem uses, not fixed calculations.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/logic/calculations/0\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose uses substantive facts not accounted for by the listed H/M inputs: compact subsets of Euclidean space are bounded; dim_H of bounded subsets of R^n is at most n; the stated Hausdorff-content/measure relationships; dimension monotonicity under Lipschitz maps; and dim_H([0,1])=1. The author-written calculation policy covers product-distance and diameter inequalities only and cannot import those results. M001/M002 do not establish these missing facts.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The declared output is the target statement dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1. S001–S003 purport to establish upper and lower bounds and combine them into equality, so the intended conclusion matches the output; the failure is validity, not a different stated target.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The proof divides according to D>0 and D=0, but does not establish that D is a finite nonnegative real or that these cases exhaust its possible Hausdorff-dimension value in the packet's stated critical-exponent convention. In particular S001's unproved D≤n is needed to justify the finite-exponent reasoning and choosing q>D. The locally fixed q, δ, s, ε and cover choices are not discharged through explicit quantified statements; the prose merely says to take limits/infima and combine bounds.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/locals/2\",\"/inference/locals/3\",\"/inference/locals/5\",\"/inference/locals/6\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The packet supplies intended bindings for both M inputs, but does not provide full ambient constructions/proofs for the applications. M001 is intended for E in Euclidean Borel space and a positive exponent below D; the bridge from the prose's real s to the NNReal exponent and the exact metric/Borel setup are only asserted. M002's countable index and indicator measurability are described, but the restricted-measure integral identity and its identification with the required cover sum are not fully established. These application concerns are additional to the earlier unsupported implication.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The output formula is explicit, but the local Hausdorff content symbol is only described as an infimum of Nat-indexed δ-cover sums; the covered set, precise admissible-cover conditions, scale convention, and exponentiation conventions are not completely stated. S002 also relies on unstated content/measure relationships. The packet does not give a fully specified local meaning adequate to check those formulas from the packet alone.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/locals/17/declaration\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/logic/primitives/1\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose introduces actual mathematical constructions beyond the registered symbols: covers of E and F, countable indexing, projections, intervals enclosing projected sets, and Hausdorff contents/measure scales. Some are named as locals, but their types/declarations do not establish existence or the stated properties. In particular r_j is declared as a witness from compactness without an input/local existence proof that supplies arbitrarily small q-cost covers, and the chosen intervals J_i are declared as a definition while the text needs their existence and width properties. x₀, by contrast, is legitimately witnessed from H001.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/4\",\"/inference/locals/7\",\"/inference/locals/8\",\"/inference/locals/11\",\"/inference/locals/12\",\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/14\",\"/inference/locals/15\",\"/inference/locals/16\",\"/inference/locals/17\",\"/inference/locals/18\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Reverse-reading factual uses reveals unlisted/unproved theorem content, beginning in S001 with compactness implying boundedness and dim_H(E)≤n. Later S002/S003 uses content-limit equivalences, Hausdorff dimension monotonicity under Lipschitz maps, and the interval's dimension. None is a direct input or fully derived local fact. M001 and M002 cannot supply these unrelated statements.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Sufficiency judgment is based only on the full packet.json and declared Yui Audit A/self-containment/format rules read for this task. Packet alone contains enough prose and input declarations to identify the first unsupported implication and reject the inference; no outside source proof or other mathematical task material was needed. This is a statement about packet-only mathematical sufficiency, not runtime/carrier authentication or canonical hash binding.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/parameters\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"First unsupported implication: H002 (E compact) ⇒ E bounded, followed by the assertion that bounded Euclidean box cube coverings imply dim_H(E)≤n. Neither implication is proved in this packet or supplied as an input. Therefore the first upper-bound step does not close.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"The content lower-bound argument imports several unproved substantive links between infinite Hausdorff measure, scale contents, cover comparisons, and Hausdorff dimension. M001 and M002 do not prove those links.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"finding\":\"Projection monotonicity for Hausdorff dimension and dim_H(I)=1 are used without a direct input or local proof. The n=0 discussion also does not prove its asserted isometry/dimension conclusion.\"}]}}"}

